WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.090
A road sign gets knocked down.

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.720
Someone puts up a new one.

3
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.040
Nobody minds.

4
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:09.760
A flag is set alight in a public
square, and people are furious.

5
00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.970
Both are just objects that
point beyond themselves.

6
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:17.700
So why does burning a flag upset people
more than knocking down a road sign?

7
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.070
In this mission, you'll meet Paul Tillich,

8
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:24.210
a German-American theologian,
and his six marks of a symbol.

9
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:28.220
Then you'll read a psalm that
calls God a rock and a fortress,

10
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.490
and ask what those words are doing.

11
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:35.000
Your mission: explain why a flag
can matter far more than a sign.
